      "text": "To determine the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert the cost from Namibian dollars to US dollars.**\n2. **Convert the cost from US dollars to Chinese yuan.**\n\n**Step 1: Convert the cost from Namibian dollars to US dollars.**\n\nWe know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 7 Namibian dollars. Therefore, the cost of the painting in US dollars can be calculated by dividing the cost in Namibian dollars by 7.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cost in US dollars} = \\frac{105 \\text{ Namibian dollars}}{7 \\text{ Namibian dollars per US dollar}} = 15 \\text{ US dollars}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Convert the cost from US dollars to Chinese yuan.**\n\nWe know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 6 Chinese yuan. Therefore, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan can be calculated by multiplying the cost in US dollars by 6.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = 15 \\text{ US dollars} \\times 6 \\text{ Chinese yuan per US dollar} = 90 \\text{ Chinese yuan}\n\\]\n\nThus, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is \\(\\boxed{90}\\).",
