      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars (N$) to Chinese yuan (C¥). We know the following exchange rates:\n\n1. 1 US dollar = 7 Namibian dollars\n2. 1 US dollar = 6 Chinese yuan\n\nFirst, we need to find out how many US dollars the painting costs in Namibian dollars. Since 1 US dollar is equivalent to 7 Namibian dollars, we can set up the following equation to find the cost of the painting in US dollars:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cost in US dollars} = \\frac{\\text{Cost in Namibian dollars}}{7}\n\\]\n\nGiven that the painting costs 105 Namibian dollars, we substitute 105 for the cost in Namibian dollars:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cost in US dollars} = \\frac{105}{7} = 15\n\\]\n\nSo, the painting costs 15 US dollars. Next, we need to convert this cost from US dollars to Chinese yuan. Since 1 US dollar is equivalent to 6 Chinese yuan, we can set up the following equation to find the cost in Chinese yuan:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = \\text{Cost in US dollars} \\times 6\n\\]\n\nSubstituting 15 for the cost in US dollars, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = 15 \\times 6 = 90\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{90}\n\\]",
